cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite this benchmark when reusing its implementation or results, and cite the original mathematical and dataset sources listed in REFERENCES.txt."
type: software
title: "Negative result: expected-median smoothing of protein contacts"
version: 0.1.0
authors:
  - name: "Rada1647"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible negative-result benchmark of binary expected-median contact
  smoothing on held-out T4 lysozyme simulations and a separate adaptive villin
  stress dataset. The construction fails the predefined primary practical-success
  criterion against validation-selected controls. Ubiquitin is excluded by a
  temporal-provenance qualification gate. AI-assisted study with five independent
  AI technical review roles; not human peer review.
keywords:
  - negative results
  - protein contacts
  - molecular dynamics
  - denoising
  - reproducibility
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Rada1647/Rada-bioinformatics-portfolio"
url: "https://github.com/Rada1647/Rada-bioinformatics-portfolio/tree/main/projects/protein-contact-benchmark"
